Networking Commands

I tried some basic commands:

ip a → shows IP addresses.

ping google.com → checks if Google is reachable.

traceroute google.com → shows the path data takes.

nslookup google.com → shows the IP behind the domain.

curl https://example.com → fetches a webpage from the terminal.

Extra practice:

bash

ip route

ping 1.1.1.1

traceroute yahoo.com

nslookup microsoft.com

curl https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1


Putting it together

I combined the commands to see how they work together.
Steps:

Use nslookup to get the IP of a domain.

Use ping to check if it’s reachable.

Use traceroute to see the path.

Use curl to talk to the server.

Practice:

bash
nslookup google.com
ping 142.250.x.x
traceroute 142.250.x.x
curl https://google.com
Another example:

bash
nslookup github.com
ping github.com
traceroute github.com
curl https://api.github.com

